<node id="&quot;INTEREST RATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Interest Rate is a financial term that signifies the percentage of a loan charged as interest to the borrower, crucial in adjustable-rate mortgages like the 5/1 ARM."&lt;SEP&gt;"Interest Rate is the percentage charged on a loan or the return on savings, which influences loan affordability and terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Interest Rate refers to the percentage charged on the loan amount, subject to adjustments based on the type of mortgage (fixed or adjustable)."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-889bb036e55402548e1f5e0fcb109226&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-783c4782c02cd021bcdf3bdbcc5f3466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1e89cab5ceec2e12a42293f598e5c33</data>
